  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The state recorded $478M in federal contract obligations for FY2027 to date. The state received 989 awards with an average award size of $483K. Obligations are down 98.1% year over year. The FY2027 to date total is partial because current-year totals are fiscal year to date. Past full fiscal years show much larger totals: FY26 was $25.2B, FY25 was $26.9B, FY24 was $26.6B, FY23 was $23.3B, and FY22 was $19.7B. The Department of Energy is the largest buyer so far, obligating $373M. FLUOR MARINE PROPULSION, LLC is the largest vendor so far, receiving $373M. Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) is the largest industry so far, with $374M in obligations. This snapshot reflects a concentrated set of awards early in the fiscal year, with a small number of large obligations driving totals to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What drove the FY2027 to date obligations in Pennsylvania?",
        "body": "The Department of Energy drove the FY2027 to date obligations with $373M. The Department of Veterans Affairs contributed $85.5M and the Department of Justice contributed $12M. FLUOR MARINE PROPULSION, LLC accounted for $373M of vendor obligations, concentrating the early-year spending."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which industries and vendors are largest so far in FY2027?",
        "body": "Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) led industries with $374M. FLUOR MARINE PROPULSION, LLC was the top vendor with $373M, followed by OLYMPUS AMERICA INC with $20.9M and CONSTELLATION NEWENERGY, INC. with $10.3M."
      }
    ]
  },
